  "id": "filarmonica_dobrado",
  "name": "Filarmônica and dobrado (Brazilian civic wind band)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Amateur civic wind bands, the sociedades filarmônicas, liras and corporações musicais, founded across Brazil from the nineteenth century and especially dense in the Recôncavo Baiano and Minas Gerais, where they play for religious processions, civic holidays, bandstand concerts and funerals and have trained generations of professional musicians. Their emblematic repertoire is the dobrado, a Brazilian quick march, alongside hymns, waltzes and arrangements. The sousaphone card stands in for the tuba and the snare-drum card for the caixa.",
  "recipe": "classic modern filarmônica and dobrado, carnival Processional. clarinet, trumpet, trombone, oompah march marching sousaphone, snare bass drum. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
